<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Peuce</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Peuce was an island in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> delta known to Greek and Roman writers, named after its pine trees and lying between the river's arms in modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romania">Romania</a>. In 335 BCE the Triballian king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syrmus">Syrmus</a> took refuge there when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-the-great">Alexander the Great</a> campaigned on the Danube, and a branch of the Bastarnae, the Peucini, took its name from it.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/peuce.jpg" alt="Peuce" width="320" height="224" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Andrein · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Danube_Delta_evolution.gif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
